<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley sat at a desk in the windowless investigators\'92 pen. The walls were a shade of colour somewhere between cinnamon latte and crushed cockroaches.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Outside, cleaners in hazmat suits would be scouring the Layer\'92s acidic residue from the building\'92s fa\'e7ades and windows. Not all buildings received such treatment; many stood like teeth from the gums of the ground, with gold Airborne crowns and gaping cavities where the Layer was the most corrosive. These eaten-out places, often stripped everything to the impervious structural columns, were where the truly abject Cloudborne lived, an underclass\'92s underclass, hidden from above and below.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley was startled from her analytic trance by another detective slamming the heel of a shoe against the wall, crushing a moderately large cockroach. Another roach fled up the wall, so the detective threw the dregs of his coffee cup at it. Hayley was thankful the season was cool; it would be months before those buggers would be flying again.\
